<title>NORWAY: TABLE - NORWAY SEAFOODS HAS NOK 313 MLN PRE-TAX LOSS.</title>
<headline>TABLE - NORWAY SEAFOODS HAS NOK 313 MLN PRE-TAX LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>			    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>  Operating revenues	 2,952	vs	2,456</p>
<p>  Operating result    minus  129	vs	   58</p>
<p>  Pre-tax result	minus  313	vs	  102</p>
<p>NOTE - Norway Seafoods ASA, the world's largest operator in catching and processing white fish, is 60 percent owned by Norwegian holding company Aker RGI ASA. A Reuters poll of five analysts forecast a first-half operating result of 147 million crowns and pre-tax profits of 116 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
